id: pm-lph0y6
title: Global flags before a subcommand corrupt guided-error command examples by treating the flag value as the command
description: "GitHub issue #984 reproduces on 2026.8.7 and 2026.8.11: pm --pm-path <tracker> plan show --json correctly identifies the missing plan id but renders the global flag value as the command in examples. Guided-error command-path recovery must use parsed command structure, never raw first-non-flag heuristics, for every host-owned global option ordering."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-12T02:57:25.496Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-12T09:06:05.160Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-12T09:05:28.705Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-12T09:05:28.705Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Global options before or after the subcommand produce identical valid help examples; option values and private filesystem paths can never be rendered as command names; focused unit and extension-forwarding regressions cover value-taking and boolean global flags; issue #984 is closed with merged evidence
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Recovery guidance now resolves the semantic subcommand with the shared bootstrap parser and never interprets global option values as command names.
expected_result: Global flags before or after a subcommand produce the same valid command-specific recovery example without exposing option values.
actual_result: "Recovery guidance selected the first non-flag argv token, so a global --pm-path value could become the displayed command name."
