comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T02:57:25.496Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for GH-984, global --pm-path placement, plan show missing-id examples, and option-value-as-command found adjacent closed recovery item pm-185870 and open grammar conformance pm-fs8q9x, but no exact owner. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/984"
  "2026-08-12T02:57:42.017Z","harness:codex","Live reproduction during duplicate search: quoting the query '--pm-path before subcommand example path value' still caused the host-owned global option to be parsed out of the search argument and produced an Unknown option refusal for the search path. This confirms the same raw-argv/global-option ambiguity reaches ordinary agent recovery workflows; no item was claimed because this session is only documenting the newly reported owner."
  "2026-08-12T08:32:06.520Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: resolveRecoveryCommandName now delegates command discovery to the bootstrap parser, so global options before or after the subcommand cannot turn tracker paths into help examples. The CLI recovery layer consumes the same public SDK primitive. Focused tests cover value and boolean globals, empty argv, and private-path exclusion."
  "2026-08-12T09:05:10.053Z","harness:codex","Exact-head PR #990 evidence at bdd380af841efce5825bc27520e2d28463e2d527: all hosted executable checks passed, including Windows Node 24, four coverage shards plus aggregate coverage, static/typecheck/compat/smoke gates, Linux/macOS runtimes, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, Codecov patch, and 11 CodSpeed benchmarks. Fresh review inventory found zero inline threads and no actionable findings. CodeRabbit and Sourcery substantive reviews were rate-limited and Greptile produced no review surface; those are recorded limitations, not approvals. Every emitted bot comment/review was individually reacted to and answered with evidence."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T08:32:06.998Z","harness:codex","Design decision: recovery guidance derives the semantic command from normalized invocation argv instead of indexing raw tokens. This keeps CLI and SDK recovery behavior identical and preserves the full attempted command only in the structured recovery receipt."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T08:32:07.526Z","harness:codex","Agent-facing help examples are a context boundary: derive them from grammar-aware command parsing, never from positional assumptions about argv, because global flag values may be private paths or unrelated identifiers."
